With the later versions of Shiny Server, you should be able use IE8 or IE9 for everything except file upload. We are only aware of the upload issue. To try out your application you can definitely do it on spark or glimmer servers; we can setup an account for you.
However, since we will be winding down Spark and Glimmer this year in favor or ShinyApps.io, I recommend that you create an account on ShinyApps and give that a try. Go to http://www.rstudio.com/shiny/hosted/ <http://www.google.com/url?q=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.rstudio.com%2Fshiny%2Fhosted%2F&sa=D&sntz=1&usg=AFQjCNEkUpoZsxXwFS9sWLqzdvy9kuyavw> for registering, and https://github.com/rstudio/shinyapps/blob/master/guide/guide.md for instructions on how to setup and get started.

Let us know if you still want an account on Glimmer/Spark.

Fereshteh

